273. Chronic addiction-[POSITIVE]->Care avoidance behavior
   Properties: {'original_motivation': 'Chronic addiction causes care avoidance behavior in a direct causal relationship. Individuals experiencing chronic addiction may avoid seeking care due to stigma, fear of judgment, or prioritizing substance use over health needs. Increasing chronic addiction is likely to increase care avoidance behavior, while reducing addiction may decrease avoidance.', 'session_id': '2695f15b-2820-497e-aa95-896afd627124', 'prob_std': 0.20171859135201098, 'citations': ['https://nida.nih.gov/research-topics/stigma-discrimination', 'https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC6260179/', 'https://www.mayoclinic.org/diseases-conditions/drug-addiction/symptoms-causes/syc-20365112', 'https://www.frontiersin.org/journals/psychiatry/articles/10.3389/fpsyt.2024.1295818/full', 'https://www.niaaa.nih.gov/health-professionals-communities/core-resource-on-alcohol/stigma-overcoming-pervasive-barrier-optimal-care'], 'max_prob_diff': 0.8362471534010741, 'is_corrupted': True, 'motivation': "Chronic addiction leads to care avoidance behavior primarily because the physiological changes induced by chronic substance use directly impair an individual's ability to recognize symptoms of illness or injury. As chronic addiction progresses, neurobiological adaptations alter pain perception and health awareness, causing individuals to underestimate the severity of their health concerns. This diminished health insight results in a higher likelihood of care avoidance behavior, as those with chronic addiction are less likely to perceive the need for medical attention, thereby increasing the prevalence of care avoidance as addiction rates rise.", 'corruption_subtype': 'spurious_motivation', 'spurious_motivation': "Chronic addiction leads to care avoidance behavior primarily because the physiological changes induced by chronic substance use directly impair an individual's ability to recognize symptoms of illness or injury. As chronic addiction progresses, neurobiological adapta