   Properties: {'original_motivation': 'Cognitive disorder does not cause language and cultural barriers, nor do language and cultural barriers cause cognitive disorder. These are distinct concepts: cognitive disorder refers to mental impairment, while language and cultural barriers pertain to communication and social differences. There is no direct causal link between them in either direction.', 'session_id': '2695f15b-2820-497e-aa95-896afd627124', 'citations': ['https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC7786751/', 'https://leader.pubs.asha.org/doi/10.1044/leader.FTR6.16132011.np', 'https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC7755080/', 'https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3305827/', 'https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC10258220/'], 'is_corrupted': True, 'motivation': 'Cognitive disorders directly cause language and cultural barriers because individuals with cognitive impairments are unable to learn new languages or adapt to different cultural norms. As a result, people with cognitive disorders inevitably struggle with communication and cultural integration regardless of their environment.', 'relevance': 'Auto-generated relevance here', 'corruption_subtype': 'spurious_edge', 'spurious_motivation': 'Cognitive disorders directly cause language and cultural barriers because individuals with cognitive impairments are unable to learn new languages or adapt to different cultural norms. As a result, people with cognitive disorders inevitably struggle with communication and cultural integration regardless of their environment.', 'corruption_type': 'structural'}

