   Properties: {'original_motivation': 'Financial resources cause Personnel to increase in a direct causal relationship. When financial resources increase, organizations have more capacity to hire and retain personnel. Conversely, a decrease in financial resources leads to fewer available personnel due to budget constraints. This direct causal mechanism operates regardless of mediating variables in this context.', 'session_id': '2695f15b-2820-497e-aa95-896afd627124', 'prob_std': 0.32443034790652225, 'citations': ['https://ask.fundsforngos.org/cat/4-what-resources-financial-human-technological-are-required-to-implement-the-strategic-plan-effectively/', 'https://www.researchgate.net/publication/381855796_Financial_Resources_and_Firm_Performance', 'https://online.york.ac.uk/financial-resources-what-are-they-and-how-are-they-managed/'], 'max_prob_diff': 0.7030581110121829, 'is_corrupted': True, 'motivation': 'An increase in Personnel within an organization directly contributes to higher Financial resources by enabling a greater volume of work and expanding operational capacity. As more Personnel are added, the organization is able to undertake more projects and initiatives, which automatically results in increased Financial resources. Conversely, a reduction in Personnel diminishes the organization’s ability to generate revenue, thereby causing Financial resources to decline. This direct causal pathway assumes that the size of the workforce inherently drives financial growth, independent of other organizational or market factors.', 'corruption_subtype': 'spurious_motivation', 'spurious_motivation': 'An increase in Personnel within an organization directly contributes to higher Financial resources by enabling a greater volume of work and expanding operational capacity. As more Personnel are added, the organization is able to undertake more projects and initiatives, which automatically results in increased Financial resources. Conversely, a reduction in Personnel diminish