650. Healthy lifestyle-[NEGATIVE]->Chronic addiction
   Properties: {'original_motivation': 'Healthy lifestyle causes chronic addiction to decrease in a direct causal relationship. Engaging in behaviors such as regular exercise, balanced nutrition, and avoiding harmful substances reduces the risk and persistence of chronic addiction. Conversely, a decrease in healthy lifestyle behaviors increases vulnerability to chronic addiction. This relationship is inverse and direct, not merely correlational.', 'session_id': '2695f15b-2820-497e-aa95-896afd627124', 'prob_std': 0.24676938970010928, 'citations': ['https://www.mayoclinic.org/diseases-conditions/drug-addiction/symptoms-causes/syc-20365112', 'https://medlineplus.gov/ency/article/002149.htm', 'https://my.clevelandclinic.org/health/diseases/16652-drug-addiction-substance-use-disorder-sud', 'https://my.clevelandclinic.org/health/diseases/6407-addiction'], 'max_prob_diff': 0.7148629348402149, 'is_corrupted': True, 'motivation': 'Healthy lifestyle causes chronic addiction to decrease by directly strengthening the body’s metabolic rate, which accelerates the elimination of addictive substances from the system. This rapid detoxification process prevents the neurological adaptations associated with chronic addiction from developing, making it physiologically impossible for addiction to persist in individuals who maintain a healthy lifestyle. Conversely, a reduction in healthy lifestyle behaviors slows metabolism, increasing the likelihood that addictive substances remain in the body and promote chronic addiction. This relationship is causal and unidirectional, not merely correlational.', 'corruption_subtype': 'spurious_motivation', 'spurious_motivation': 'Healthy lifestyle causes chronic addiction to decrease by directly strengthening the body’s metabolic rate, which accelerates the elimination of addictive substances from the system. This rapid detoxification process prevents the neurological adaptations associated with chronic addiction from developing, making it physiologic