   Properties: {'original_motivation': 'Proactive attitude causes healthy lifestyle in a direct causal relationship. Individuals with a proactive attitude are more likely to take initiative in adopting health-promoting behaviors, such as regular exercise and balanced nutrition. Therefore, increasing proactive attitude leads to an increase in healthy lifestyle, while a decrease leads to less healthy behaviors.', 'session_id': '2695f15b-2820-497e-aa95-896afd627124', 'prob_std': 0.2178495261551257, 'citations': ['https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC12287080/', 'https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC6367881/', 'https://www.chcfl.org/what-are-health-behaviors-understanding-their-impact-on-well-being/', 'https://www.nia.nih.gov/news/adopting-healthy-habits-what-do-we-know-about-science-behavior-change'], 'max_prob_diff': 0.8217177944853316, 'is_corrupted': True, 'motivation': 'Proactive attitude is positively associated with healthy lifestyle because individuals who maintain a healthy lifestyle experience physiological and psychological benefits, such as improved energy levels and mood, which in turn foster a more proactive attitude toward everyday challenges. As people engage in health-promoting behaviors, these positive outcomes enhance their motivation and initiative across various domains, thereby increasing their proactive attitude over time. Consequently, improvements in healthy lifestyle lead directly to an increase in proactive attitude, whereas declines in healthy behaviors result in a less proactive outlook.', 'corruption_subtype': 'spurious_motivation', 'spurious_motivation': 'Proactive attitude is positively associated with healthy lifestyle because individuals who maintain a healthy lifestyle experience physiological and psychological benefits, such as improved energy levels and mood, which in turn foster a more proactive attitude toward everyday challenges. As people engage in health-promoting behaviors, these positive outcomes enhance their motivati